.SS Abstract
Defines \f[CR]IS__COMMA_OPERATOR__SUPPORTED\f[R] if the compiler
supports the comma operator.
.SS Content
.IP
.EX
#define IS__COMMA_OPERATOR__SUPPORTED
.EE
.PP
The comma operator refers to the \f[CR](,)\f[R] operator in macros or
expressions, used to evaluate multiple expressions in sequence and
return the last.
.PP
\f[B]Example\f[R]:
.IP
.EX
#ifdef IS__COMMA_OPERATOR__SUPPORTED
int a = (b++, funct(), c = 42, b += c, 66); \f[I]// Performs all actions and returns 66\f[R]
#else
b++;
funct();
c = 42;
b += c;
int a = 66;
#endif
.EE
